{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["Can a rebellious fool who defies his Maker succeed? In his wholeness honor Him. An arrow will split a reprobate's skull. See and turn back, and set your heart on all Pharaoh's words in the portion of Beshalach." "<b>When he sent.</b> The vav [is conjunctive]. And naḥam [has] no dagesh in the peh; it is rapheh in the language of Ishmael. It is known that from Egypt to Jerusalem by way of the land of the Philistines is not a great distance; it is about a ten-day journey on the direct route. And were it not so, how could the tribes have come with their donkeys to Egypt if the way were very far? What would have sufficed for them and their donkeys to eat, and on their return to bring provisions for their households?" "<b>For it is near.</b> R. Moses said: even though it is near — and like it, in my view: \"for it is a stiff-necked people\" (below 34:9); \"Heal my soul, for I have sinned against You\" (Psalms 41:5); \"for he has chariots of iron\" (Joshua 17:16). And in my view there is no need, for its sense is why Elohim did not lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines — because it is near. So He led them by a far way, so that they would not see war and say, \"Let us appoint a head and return to Egypt.\"" "And let us know that HaShem knows the future without doubt, and He knew that they would reconsider if He led them by the way of the land of the Philistines. And He said, \"Lest the people reconsider,\" for the Torah speaks in the language of human beings, so that those who study will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:18.147215667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}